# Regression testing

New features and refactors must **not break existing behavior**. Treat regression protection as part of the feature. This rule supplements `plan-execution.mdc` and `definition-of-done.mdc`: every verification step here must pass (or be explicitly blocked with reason) before declaring work done.

## Mindset

- **Preserve contracts**: HTTP status codes, the `AppError` JSON envelope (`api-error-shape.mdc`), the canonical `Event` shape (`canonical-event-schema.mdc`), tenant scoping (`tenant-isolation.mdc`), RBAC gates, migration behavior, and user-visible globe/search flows must still work—unless the task documents a breaking change and updates all consumers in the same work.
- **Test the blast radius, not just the diff**: ask what existing paths your change touches (shared `core` helpers, middleware, RBAC, DB/PostGIS/vector queries, shared types, connectors, scoring) and run checks for those areas.
- **Add a guardrail when you fix a bug**: extend or add a test so the same regression cannot return silently.

## Test inventory (this repo)

| Area | Automated checks | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **API (`crates/api`)** | `cargo test -p geos-api` | Requires `DATABASE_URL` (Postgres+PostGIS). Integration tests cover auth/MFA, tenant isolation, RBAC, events/relations, search, exports. |
| **Core (`crates/core`)** | `cargo test -p geos-core` | Domain model, canonical schema, impact scoring, error mapping. |
| **Workers (`crates/workers`)** | `cargo test -p geos-workers` | Connector normalization, dedupe/entity resolution, enrichment, correlation. |
| **CLI (`crates/cli`)** | `cargo test -p geos-cli` | Add tests when CLI behavior changes. |
| **Rust quality** | `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo fmt --check` | Run on Rust changes; fix new warnings. |
| **Frontend (`frontend`)** | `pnpm lint`, `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit`, `pnpm build` | Build + lint catch type/import regressions. |
| **Frontend e2e** | `pnpm test:e2e` (Playwright) | Exercise critical UI paths (auth, globe load, filter, search). |
| **Migrations** | startup / `cargo test -p geos-api` | New migrations only (`api-sqlx-migrations.mdc`); verify existing routes still work against migrated schema. |

## Verification matrix (by change type)

Run **all rows that apply**; when in doubt, run the broader set.

| You changed... | Required checks |
| --- | --- |
| **API handler, middleware, auth, RBAC, tenant scoping** | Full `cargo test -p geos-api`; add/extend integration test when behavior is HTTP-visible or tenant/permission-gated |
| **Canonical `Event` / core domain** | `cargo test -p geos-core` + schema-drift check; bump JSON schema + TS types + migration together |
| **SQL schema or PostGIS/vector queries** | New migration file; API/worker tests; manually verify affected map/list/detail flows if no test yet |
| **Error responses or status codes** | API tests; confirm frontend client still parses errors |
| **Connector / ingestion / correlation** | `cargo test -p geos-workers`; verify idempotent upsert + dedupe (`connector-contract.mdc`) |
| **AI enrichment / provider** | `cargo test -p geos-workers`/`core`; confirm air-gapped/skippable path still works (`ai-provider-abstraction.mdc`) |
| **Frontend pages, hooks, globe, API client** | `pnpm lint` + `tsc --noEmit` + `pnpm build`; Playwright smoke of login + the changed view + one adjacent flow |
| **Shared types / config contract** | Rust tests + frontend build; grep consumers and spot-check |
| **CLI commands** | `cargo test -p geos-cli`; manual run against a dev stack |
| **Cross-cutting refactor** | Full workspace tests + frontend lint/build + clippy on touched crates |

## Adding regression tests (required unless blocked)

- New API endpoint or changed status/permission/tenant behavior -> integration test.
- Bug fix where a test would have caught it -> add that test in the same change set.
- New permission key or role behavior -> verify grant/deny in API tests.
- Do **not** weaken or delete existing tests to make new code pass without user approval.

## When tests cannot run

- **No Postgres / `DATABASE_URL`**: run `cargo clippy` and frontend lint/build; clearly tell the user which integration tests were not executed and provide the exact command.
- **Blocked by environment**: document the blocker, run what you can, never imply full coverage.
- **User explicitly skips tests**: honor only for the current request; still note the risk.

## Report evidence

Name commands run and outcomes (e.g. `cargo test -p geos-api`: 42 passed; `pnpm build`: success). For manual smokes, list paths exercised.
